interview with Microsoft for an Azure DevOps / Cloud role and the level of depth in the discussion was truly inspiring.

The interview process was structured into 3 comprehensive rounds, each testing not just technical expertise but also architectural thinking, governance, AI integration, and business alignment.

🔹 1️⃣ Round 1 – Azure & DevOps Fundamentals
The discussion focused heavily on:

Azure Cloud Adoption Framework (CAF)

Landing Zones & Management Groups

Azure Governance (RBAC, Policies, Blueprints)

Azure Data Factory & Integration Runtime

Hub-and-Spoke Networking & VNet design

Terraform (state management, backend config, imports)

Azure DevOps Pipelines & Agents

Docker & Containerization

AI Services in Azure

This round tested real-world implementation experience, not just theory.

🔹 2️⃣ Round 2 – Deep Technical & Architecture
This round was intense and scenario-driven. Topics included:

Designing Azure Landing Zones at scale

Hub & Spoke vs Mesh topology decisions

Availability Sets vs Availability Zones

Custom Azure Policies with JSON logic

Azure Monitor & Diagnostic Settings

NSG troubleshooting scenarios

DNS resolution & Private Endpoints

Application Gateway vs Load Balancer

Advanced Terraform practices (state conflicts, refresh, for_each, naming validation)

AKS deployment strategies & Helm

AI integration using Python & Azure AI services

The focus was on decision-making ability, governance strategy, scalability, and optimization.

🔹 3️⃣ Round 3 – Hiring Manager (Business + Strategy + AI Vision)
This was beyond technical skills. It included:

End-to-end migration lifecycle

Migrating 400+ servers to Azure

Mainframe migration strategy

AI licensing & cost justification

CEO-level strategic thinking

Solution architecture & ROI discussion

Real customer AI use cases & automation outcomes

This round evaluated leadership mindset, consulting skills, cost optimization, and business alignment.

Key Takeaways
✅ Microsoft evaluates depth, not buzzwords
✅ Strong fundamentals in Azure governance & networking are critical
✅ Terraform & IaC must be practical, not theoretical
✅ AI integration knowledge is becoming mandatory
✅ Business justification & architecture thinking matter as much as technical skills

If you are preparing for Azure DevOps / Cloud Architect roles, focus on:

Azure CAF & Landing Zones
Enterprise-scale networking
Terraform advanced concepts
AKS & container strategies
Azure AI services
Migration lifecycle & cost modeling
